        "iid": 4018,
        "project_id": 34675721,
        "title": "feat(api): detect Kiro terminal sessions",
        "description": "## Description\n\nDetect Kiro IDE terminal sessions as `kiro-terminal` when `TERM_PROGRAM` equals `kiro`, using the existing case-insensitive terminal fallback. Preserve the current detection precedence and ignore unrelated prefixes.\n\nThe terminal signal is evidenced by the installer shell-integration condition in [Kiro #7169](https://github.com/kirodotdev/Kiro/issues/7169). Dedicated Kiro CLI and GitHub Copilot signals remain unverified, so this contribution covers terminal detection and does not close the broader issue.\n\n## Related Issues\n\nRelated to #8331\n\n## How has this been tested?\n\n- New positive regression cases failed before the implementation.\n- Full `internal/api` tests and required Lefthook pre-commit and pre-push checks passed: build, lint with zero issues, 4,074 reverse-dependency tests with 8 skipped, and structural checks.\n- Added lowercase, mixed-case and false-positive cases.\n- Tested on macOS arm64 with Go 1.27.1; direct Kiro runtime verification was unavailable.\n\nAI assistance was used to prepare the change. The code received independent review and local testing.\n\n\\/copy_metadata #8331",
