      {
        "id": 544439860,
        "iid": 4016,
        "project_id": 34675721,
        "title": "fix(glrepo): skip fork candidates without local remotes",
        "description": "## Description\n\nWith prompts disabled, `glab mr create` can panic when a local fork's parent is itself a fork: `HeadRepo` selects the API-only parent and returns a typed-nil `*Remote`. Skip fork candidates whose local remote lookup fails, and preserve the existing first-remote fallback.\n\nAdd a fork-of-a-fork regression that asserts a non-nil head repository with the expected name and host. This change addresses #8567; the distinct unrelated-fork selection behavior in #8382 remains outside its scope.\n\n## Related Issues\n\nResolves #8567\n\n## How has this been tested?\n\n- The new regression failed before the resolver change.\n- `Test_HeadRepo`, required Lefthook pre-commit and pre-push checks passed.\n- `make check`: 5,502 tests passed, 9 skipped. Full lint reported six existing findings in untouched documentation, Duo ask, and dependency-firewall files; lint against this branch's changes passed. The same findings were reproduced on unchanged `main`.\n- Tested on macOS arm64 with Go 1.27.1.\n\nAI assistance was used to prepare the change. The code received independent review and local testing.\n\n\\/copy_metadata #8567",
